  "title": "Debug: the last direction",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## One binding, many callbacks\n\nA loop with `var i` (or one `let dir` you overwrite) makes every callback see the **last** value. The fox repeats the last dir.\n\nFix it: `let` in the loop, or `dirs.forEach((dir) => { ... })` so each callback has its own `dir`."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "var-loop",
      "promptMd": "Three `var` callbacks scheduled in a loop over `east, south, west` often all see…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "each",
          "md": "Their own dir from that iteration",
          "misconceptionId": "closure-copies-value"
        },
        {
          "id": "last",
          "md": "The last dir after the loop finishes"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "last"
    },
